imagecache: do not replace a cached image when the write failed.

tvheadend/tvheadend#2323, our PR, one commit.  Drop this patch once it is
merged.  Reported as tvheadend/tvheadend#2322.

imagecache_new_contents() ignores the result of fwrite and of fclose and
carries on regardless.  On ENOSPC or EIO it unlinks the image that was still
valid, stores the sha1 of the content it meant to write, renames the partial
file into its place, and persists that metadata.

The check at the top of the same function then makes the damage permanent:

    if (!empty && memcmp(sha1, img->sha1, 20) == 0)
      return 0; /* identical */

The stored sha1 matches the content that was supposed to be there, so the next
fetch of that image returns early as "identical" and never rewrites it.  The
entry stays corrupt while advertising itself as current, and nothing repairs it
short of deleting the file or clearing the cache.  A channel or EPG icon that
stays broken long after the disk-full condition is gone is the visible symptom.

Found while building for the older Synology targets in SynoCommunity#7391,
which replaces the ageing GCC there with an 8.5 overlay: those sysroots' glibc
declares fwrite with __wur and tvheadend builds with -Werror, so the ignored
return became fatal.  Current glibc marks fread with __wur but not fwrite, so
on an ordinary modern build nothing is reported at all -- checked with GCC 12.2
against glibc 2.36, clean even under -O2 -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=2
-Werror=unused-result.  The defect does not depend on any of that.

The number 500 was the http digest patch (#2273), merged as 5a32b04b9 and
dropped; it is reused here for an unrelated PR of its own, as each upstream PR
owns a hundred.  200 is the other imagecache PR (#2160) and does not touch this
function, so the two are independent and order does not matter.
--- src/imagecache.c.orig
+++ src/imagecache.c
@@ -268,8 +268,17 @@ imagecache_new_contents ( imagecache_image_t *img,
   if (!(fp = tvh_fopen(tpath, "wb")))
     return 1;
 
-  fwrite(data, dsize, 1, fp);
-  fclose(fp);
+  if (dsize && fwrite(data, dsize, 1, fp) != 1) {
+    tvherror(LS_IMAGECACHE, "unable to write file '%s'", tpath);
+    fclose(fp);
+    unlink(tpath);
+    return 1;
+  }
+  if (fclose(fp)) {
+    tvherror(LS_IMAGECACHE, "unable to close file '%s'", tpath);
+    unlink(tpath);
+    return 1;
+  }
   unlink(path);
   tvh_mutex_lock(&imagecache_lock);
   memcpy(img->sha1, sha1, 20);
